\begin{align*}
(-2+\sqrt{b})(-2-\sqrt{b})&=1\\
4-2\sqrt{b}-2\sqrt{b}+b&=1\\
b-4\sqrt{b}+3&=0
\end{align*}

So the maximum value of $|(z - 1)^2 (z + 1)|$ is $\sqrt{(3-2\sqrt{2}(-\frac{1}{2}))(7-4(-\frac{1}{2})^2)}=\sqrt{(3+\sqrt{2})(7-\frac{1}{2})}=\boxed{\sqrt{\frac{25}{2}}}$.

# Answer

